speechtext:
Madam Speaker, I rise on a matter of urgent and pressing necessity under the provisions of Standing Order 43.
In view of increasing problems in the footwear industry as a result of the government's refusal to meet the demands made by the industry, in view of the fact that the minister responsible stated yesterday that he would be in a position to make a decision after meeting with his provincial counterparts on June 21, and with a view to safeguarding existing jobs, I move, seconded by the hon. member for Cambridge (Mr. Speyer);
That this House unanimously urge the minister in question to make his decision not later than June 30.
